  "rationale": "The question asks for biochemical inhibition of purified DNA-PK catalytic subunit (P78527), so cell-based steps (cell-prepare, cell-expose, cell-detect) are excluded: cellular viability would not establish target-specific causality. An ADP-Glo luminescent kinase assay (proto:kinase_biochem_lum) directly measures catalytic activity via ADP generation, matching the retained measurement examples of DNA-PK inhibition assays (CHEMBL1243970, CHEMBL1118579). ATP at 10 uM is the only reaction condition with packet support (CHEMBL1243970, document CHEMBL1240340). The concentration series (100 uM top, 3-fold, 10 points, triplicate) is a design assumption chosen to span likely potency without relying on any remembered or withheld IC50 for CHEMBL104468; the retained IC50s for other compounds (60-1700 nM) are contextual only and were not used to estimate this compound's potency.",
